            <h3>1. No Doctor-Patient Relationship</h3>
            <p>
                Use of Health Hub, its health calculators, nutritional engines, fitness estimators, drug safety checkers, and pediatric tools does not establish a doctor-patient, practitioner-patient, or confidential therapeutic relationship between you and Health Hub, its developers, or its medical content contributors.
            </p>

            <h3 style="margin-top: 1.75rem;">2. Not Medical Advice or Diagnosis</h3>
            <p>
                All physiological equations, scoring models, and formulas utilized on this platform (including, but not limited to, Mifflin-St Jeor, Devine, Harris-Benedict, AHA Blood Pressure Stages, CDC Growth Percentiles, openFDA labeling, CURB-65, MELD, and GCS scores) represent theoretical mathematical models and population statistical averages.
            </p>
            <p>
                These models <strong>cannot account for your unique genetics, medical history, clinical laboratory tests, underlying chronic conditions, medication interactions, or physical pathology</strong>. You must never rely on calculator results as a confirmed medical diagnosis or definitive assessment of your health status.
            </p>

            <h3 style="margin-top: 1.75rem;">3. Mandatory Professional Consultation</h3>
            <p>
                <strong>Always seek the advice of a board-certified physician, licensed medical doctor, registered dietitian, or qualified healthcare provider</strong> before:
            </p>
            <ul style="padding-left: 1.5rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                <li>Starting, modifying, or stopping any prescription medication, over-the-counter drugs, or dietary supplements.</li>
                <li>Initiating extreme caloric deficits, fasting schedules, keto diets, or intensive exercise programs.</li>
                <li>Making clinical decisions regarding pregnancy, infant feeding, pediatric dosage, or chronic disease management.</li>
                <li>Interpreting blood pressure readings, glucose metrics, or cardiovascular risk indicators.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 style="margin-top: 1.75rem;">4. Emergency Medical Situations</h3>
            <p>
                Health Hub is NOT designed for medical emergencies or acute clinical situations. <strong>If you believe you or someone in your care is experiencing a medical emergency (such as severe chest pain, shortness of breath, sudden weakness or numbness, severe allergic reaction, or acute trauma), IMMEDIATELY CALL YOUR LOCAL EMERGENCY SERVICES (911 / 112 / 999) OR PROCEED TO THE NEAREST EMERGENCY ROOM.</strong>
